Where the source code is
------------------------
Each release (https://github.com/qcom-toolbox/Banana-OS/releases, build-N)
has, next to its images and java.bpk, Banana_OS-sources.tar: the complete
corresponding source of every program in them - the upstream source
archives exactly as the build scripts fetched them (SOURCES.txt lists each
one with its SHA-256), the trees taken from git, and the Banana OS
repository at the release's tag (its build scripts, patches and
configuration, and Banana OS itself). It stays available for as long as the
release's images are offered there. The same files can be rebuilt by
running the ports/<name>/build.sh scripts of that tag.
